<title>POLAND: All Polish minimum T-bill prices down at tender.</title>
<headline>All Polish minimum T-bill prices down at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills fell at today's primary auction on total demand of 549 million zlotys against a one billion zloty offer, the Finance Ministry said.  </p>
<p>The treasury sold 386 million zlotys worth of bills.</p>
<p>It also lowered next Monday's primary T-bill tender offer by 200 million to 800 million zlotys.</p>
<p>    T-bill	   8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    ---     95.28    90.90     ---     83.20</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.30)  (91.02)    ---    (83.25)</p>
<p>   new max price    ---     95.50    91.10     ---     83.35</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.47)  (91.14)    ---    (83.48)</p>
<p>   offer		---     200.0    300.0     ---     500.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    ---     232.9     80.3     ---     235.3</p>
<p>   bids accepted    ---     200.0     63.3     ---     122.8</p>
<p>   next auction     ---     300.0    100.0     ---     400.0</p>
<p>   (pvs announced offer)    200.0    300.0     ---     500.0</p>
<p>Note: Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
